oved","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:f92f16060cfd47a332dcbce77e808593436b18003eca71b7bd94a5db99a4cecc","file":"preprints/Uniform-Permanence-in-Weakly-Reversible-Mass-Action-Systems-October-5-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex","line":43,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"1bced76bde3af6481cb218a48f030b4aa4564b2ea60dc8bae4df0edf03803595","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/Uniform-Permanence-in-Weakly-Reversible-Mass-Action-Systems-October-5-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:f92f16060cfd47a332dcbce77e808593436b18003eca71b7bd94a5db99a4cecc","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Uniform-Permanence-in-Weakly-Reversible-Mass-Action-Systems-October-5-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex#L43"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{thm:main}\nLet $C\\subset\\Z_{\\geq0}^d$ be finite, let $R\\subset C\\times C$ be\nweakly reversible, and fix positive rate constants in\n\\eqref{eq:mass-action}. For every positive stoichiometric class $P$ there\nis a nonempty compact convex set $K_P\\subset P$ with the following\nproperties. Every initial point $x^0\\in P$ gives a unique global positive\nsolution, and there is a finite $T(x^0)\\geq0$ such that\n\\[\n  x(t)\\in K_P\\qquad(t\\geq T(x^0)).\n\\]\nMoreover, $K_P$ is forward invariant. In particular, there is\n$\\eps_P\\in(0,1)$, depending only on the network, the fixed rates, and\n$P$, such that every such solution satisfies\n\\begin{equation}\\label{eq:uniform-bounds}\n  \\eps_P\\leq x_i(t)\\leq\\eps_P^{-1}\n  \\qquad(1\\leq i\\leq d,\\ t\\geq T(x^0)).\n\\end{equation}"}
